From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 17:25:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 045/117] PCI: apple: add H9P Wi-Fi port lifecycle

Extend the T8010 H9P host bridge with the firmware-derived PHY,
power-control, DART reload, PERST and retry ordering needed for the
BCM4355 port while preserving the generic PCI host and MSI paths.

IRQSTAT and IRQMASK are read from the same per-port register bank, and
set bits in IRQMASK suppress their sources. Mask all sources, clear
pending W1C status with a readback, install the intended unmasked-source
pattern, and only then enable the Linux IRQ. The handler acknowledges
active status with a W1C write and readback so the level interrupt
cannot remain asserted.

The H9P Link Capability dwords are read-only. Treat max-link-speed = <1>
as the real Gen1 contract and limit only the SLS fields returned by the
local H9P config-read path for that port. Generic PCI config access and
retraining code remain unchanged.

Create and destroy endpoint pwrctrl devices under host ownership, defer
until all required suppliers are bound, balance clock and endpoint power
cleanup, and reload retained DART translation state before PERST
releases the endpoint.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: f6fdf13deb53ebf349bac8ed88766f0dade4427e
